{"text": "Gregory W. Gray\n\nSUMMARY\n\nSeasoned academic executive with a demonstrated track record of leadership, motivation and\naccomplishment. Especially adept at working successfully across organizational boundaries with\nhighly diverse constituencies. A high integrity administrator with polished skills in fund raising,\nfacilities management, student recruitment and program development.\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\nRiverside Community College District\nChancellor \u2014 July 2009 \u2014 present\n\nThree college community college district\n2,000+ employees\n$160M Budget\n$350M construction bond\nReport to a 5 member, at large, elected board\nAnnual credit enrollment tops 100,000\nService area exceeds 1.3 million residents and 440 square miles\n\nMajor Achievements:\n\nReorganized RCCD into a 3 college multi-college district\nNegotiated a successful project labor agreement\nEstablished study abroad program in China\nDeveloped enrollment management task force to deal with \u201cunfunded\u201d\nFTES and right-sizing the institution\nAchieved full ACCJC Accreditation status for both Moreno Valley and\nNorco Colleges\nEstablished service learning program at all three colleges\nArchitect for \u201c100 at a 100\u201d fundraising campaign\nReduced budget by over $45M without layoffs or furloughs of full-time\npersonnel\nCreated Chancellor's Circle for Innovation\nEstablished Center for Green Technologies\nSecured largest private gift in the history of the District - $5M\n$3M Gates grant to improve high school completion and attending\ncommunity college\n$3M NFS grant to establish National Center for Logistics Education\n\nMiami Dade College Kendall Campus\nPresident \u2014 September 2006 \u2014 July 2009\n\nGregory W. Gray\n\nApproximately 65,000 annual unduplicated headcount\n1,700 employees\n$60M Budget",
